def write_docs(r, rounds):
    b = r['practice_contrast']
    q = r['pressure_summary']
    p = r['preparation_summary']
    v = r['verification']
    source_max = r['surface_summary']['source_surface_max_error_mm']
    text = _release_expand(f"""# Measured tooth surface through the preparation chain\n\nRun from this directory: `./run_all.sh` . The command controls frozen hashes, reads local original surfaces, run geometric and load-related counter-tests and creates `figures/demo.png` and `results.json` . No data is retrieved. Code dependencies: Python3 , NumPy , SciPy , trimesh , scikit-image, matplotlib and rtree; used versions are available in `raw/ENVIRONMENT.json` .\n\nThe idea is to use the measured surface of the tooth before preparation as the crown's outside and keep its original triangles through export. The preparation has its own representation. A generic anatomy does not have to replace already known anatomy. Leave-one -tooth-out means here **ta Output and re-insert a tooth in bite with exported measured outside**. The surface of the tooth is inputs; the attempt does not predict a unknown tooth or a pre-prepared form but previously scan.\n\n| Query and resolution | Results | Reference / validity |\n|---|---|---|\n| Preserved original surface? PER_POINT, 24 tooth regions | maximum export error {source_max:.3g} mm ; contact number and unchanged mode | Original Bits2Bites triangles in registered bite; dental labels from X11, not independently validated in this domain |\n| New surface information contribution, PER_SURFACE_REGION, 12 historical dental case | median mask-IoU {b['median_practice_IoU']:.4f} → {b['median_candidate_IoU']:.4f}; median generic mode error {b['median_practice_centroid_error_mm']:.3f} mm | Same original gate and antagonist; post-replay of frozen X18 -prior, no commercial CAD evaluation |\n| Number of proximity regions, PER_SURFACE_REGION | 58 regions in 24 teeth in 0,1 mm band and 0,15 mm sampling | Geometric proximity, no pressure measurement; 14 / 24 tooth regions break penetration limit 0,03 mm |\n| Can tooth force reduce unknown contact load voltage variation? PER_TOOTH | {q['old_shape_ratio_range'][0]:.2f}–{q['old_shape_ratio_range'][1]:.2f}× persists; decrease 0% | Original X18 -roof, linear FE with adopted support/material; not stress in the new preparation |\n| Which measuring channels are missing? PER_SURFACE_REGION | Total tooth force requires additional n − 1 contact integrals for full force distribution ; with two moment remains n − rank(G) | Exact rank/affin polytope under the model; CoP-measurement and laboratory calibration NOT_RUN |\n| Preparation geometry, PER_TOOTH , virtual specimen case 127 / FDI36 | R1 normaloffset:24/24 veck; R4 implicit iso:1 incorrect edge; R5:0 incorrect edges at 1,205mm erosion | Closed geometric specimen ; virtual base and single-sided deposit volume are Closures, not measured preparation |\n| Replaykontroller | {v['check_count']} controls {v['status']} | Error injections: surface displacement, wrong source/pressure integral, confused jaw / support , wrong resultant, missing facet |\n\nThe pressure range for each contact region is available in `rounds/R2.json` : p_j = F_tand · α_j / A_j , α ≥ 0 and Σ α= 1 . The lower jaw's absolute forces comes from [Hattori1996 , Table1's 113 ](https://doi.org/10.7144/sgf.2.111). The upper jaw's relative signals come from [Ferrato2017 , Table3's 83 ]( https://doi.org/10.11138/ads/2017.8.2.079 ; they summarize to 93% and do not normalise. The absolute pressure of the upper jaw is given per N unknown arc force. Mean ± 2 SD is a descriptive population scenario, no individual confidence limit. The contact's own pressure profile is assumed to be uniform; actual peak pressure is missing boundary from this data.\n\nThe power tables can change absolute load but cannot determine how the dental power is distributed among the contact regions. Scaled all contact voltages with the same tooth force , the ratio between worst and area-weighted tensile voltage remains the same. Hypothetical moment data lowers the conditional upper ratio to 1,00 – 3,68 × in the old model case, but these elements have not been measured. `code/compare_measurement.py` and `MEASUREMENT_SPEC.md` indicate the future measurement interface.\n\nWhat does not holds : the bite registration is not a loaded contact measurement, FDI and cervical margin lack local reference , 28 / 28 support lines cannot provide verified axial molar/premolar stiffness, and no pressure / strain measurements is available for these specimen . Den slutna preparationen bevisar numerisk exportbarhet inom sin virtuella volym. It proves neither clinical fitness, remaining dentin, actual margin, cement fit or strength. SDF is a voxel distance to the defined insertion volume; continuous failure to actual tooth volume is UNKNOWN. Scanner and label errors are not included in 0,1 mm voxel resolution.\n\nData/licence: [ Bits2Bites_v01 ](https://ditto.ing.unimore.it/bits2bites/) CC BY - NC - SA according to briefing and upstream project; local ZIP :en contains no separate license file, public page confirms registered RAS - scans but does not display license text. X11 : s labels have upstream training on Teeth3DS ; its exact local dataset license is not verified, see X11 . No Teeth3DS areas or personal data are exported. ToothFairy2 , mandible defects and second datasets are not used. Primary articles are referenced and saved PDF :s are bound with hash; their texts are not reproduced in the demonstration.\n\nExport: `127_36_regular_implicit_preparation.stl` and the exact `*_external.stl` are below `@DENTAL_WORK_ROOT@/X18b_prep_surface/`. The old normal offset crown is a preserved failure; it should not be used as a passed construction. These are two geometric parts, no finished clinical crown. Arrays and STL together take {r['data_bytes'] / 1000000.0:.1f}MB, with SHA-256 in `raw/DATA_MANIFEST.json`.\n\nFull cost is available in `results.json`. Existing X11 -fit and research discovery cost are UNKNOWN and are not counted as free. Numerical equality with the original surface/full enumeration is a control line, no claim about algorithm news. Status: PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.\n""")
    (H / 'README_DEMO.md').write_text(text)
    (H / 'RESULTS.md').write_text(text.replace('# Measured tooth surface through the preparation chain', '# Result X18b – measured outside preserved, regional printing information missing', 1))
    (H / 'HANDOFF.md').write_text(f"X18b : six designs completed, PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW . Read README_DEMO.md/results.json , run ./run_all.sh .\n\nR1 source-carrier SURFACE_PASS : 24 / 24,58 proximity regions. Exact Outside, 0mm export error, 0 number/mode error against the original tooth. LOTO is re-institution with known preoperative surface, not blind form precision. 14/24 is rejected as physical bite pose at 0,03 mm-gate; worst projected gap − 0,334626936 mm. 24/24 normal offset preparations are folded; 17/24 source-shells have nonmanifold extraction woundary.\nR2 NEGATIVE_PRESSURE_IDENTIFIABILITY : Hattori Table1 mandibulary N and Ferrato Table3 upper percent read directly; no rescaling/transfers. Intra-tooth shape ratio 1,896449787 – 14,057396213 × persists, 0% reduction. 28 / 28 support lines are rejected for axial posterior k. Pressure intervals per region are scenario/close; physical contact force and stress UNKNOWN .\nR3 CALIBRATION_OPERATOR_PASS : total+ two moment leaves 0,1,4,3,0,0,0,3 free power dimensions on 8 original sites. Extra patchintegraler identifierar full vektor. Hypothetical area-CoP, no measurement ; minimum for full contact load, not proven minimum for maximum stress only.\nR4 IMPLICIT_SPECIMEN_FAIL : distance erosion of virtual deposit volume gave 1 edge with 4 facets at the exact 1,2 mm level. R5 REGULAR_SPECIMEN_PASS : conservative 1,205 mm level gives 0 error edges; removed facet gives 3 error edges. Voxel depth control error 0,031665486 mm; actually prep/cervical/ PDL /pulp reference UNKNOWN .\nR6 COMMON_GRID_INFORMATION_PASS : 12 historical mandibulary cases compared to original gate. Generic prior medianIoU 0,0079365 against measured outside 1,0 ; original scan is reference . Historical replay after R1 , no new held-out anatomy prediction. Old X18 - preparation /site-leakage error is retained as upstream restriction.\n\nNext essential construction: independent tooth and cervical boundary entry, registered real pre/post preparation, same loaded bite with spatially calibrated pressure and separate resultant. Use frozen predictions + code/compare_measurement.py without readjustment. If only force +CoP is measured, run saved nullspace and requests the specified extra patch integrals; do not fill with area weight as measurement . Before this, a local next round can test source-envelope convergence/support selection but must not call it physical validation.\n\nGraph dispatch is available for DENT - VAL - OCCLUSAL - REGIONAL - FORCES . Saknad coverage: DENT-CROWN-PREOPERATIVE-SURFACE-CARRIER, DENT-PREP-CERVICAL-MARGIN-MEASUREMENT, DENT-LOAD-REGISTERED-PATCH-PRESSURE-CALIBRATION. GRAPH_FEEDBACK links at the finest quantity level with SIMULTANEOUS / HANDOVER ; no native/generated graphs modified.\n\nData {r['data_bytes'] / 1000000.0:.1f}MB on the games disk, hash manifest raw/DATA_MANIFEST.json. ≤ 1 thread in numericals,< 1 GB RSS in executed steps, no GPU /heavy jobs/sub-agents/mail/push. Full fit/discovery cost delvis UNKNOWN. Failed gates and frozen versions preserved.\n")
